G1506.def:
εἰλικρινής, -ές, 
[in LXX: Wi 72^ kB * ;] 
unalloyed, pure (Lat. sincerus; see DCG, ii, 635a); 
__(a) of unmixed substances; 
__(b) of abstract ideas; 
__(with) of ethical purity: Philippiens 1:10, 2 Pierre 3:1.†
SYN.: ἁγνός (which see), καθαρός, cf. Tr., Syn.: §lxxxv; DB, iv, 176a; Cremer, 378; Westc. on 1 Jean 3:3.

G1510.def:
εἰμί, 
with various uses and significations, like the English verb to be. 
__I. As substantive verb. 
__1. Of persons and things, to be, exist: Actes 17:28, Jean 1:1, 8:58, 17:5, al; ὁ ὢν καὶ ὁ ἦν (for past ptcp.), Apocalypse 1:4, 8, 4:8, 11:17, 16:5 (see Swete, Ap., 5; M, Pr., 228); τὰ (μὴ) ὄντα, Romains 4:17, 1 Corinthiens 1:28. 
__2. Of times, events, etc., to be, happen, take place: Matthieu 24:3, Marc 14:2, 15:42, Luc 21:23, Jean 4:6, 23, 5:10, al. 
__3. to be present, be in a place, have come: Matthieu 2:13, 15, Marc 1:45, 5:21, 15:40, Luc 1:80, 5:29, Jean 7:30, al.; before εἰς, Marc 2:1; before ἐκ, (ἐξ), Matthieu 1:20, 21:25, Marc 11:30, Jean 3:31, al. 
__4. Impers., ἔστι, ἦν, etc.; 
__(a) there is (Fr. il y a), was, etc.: Matthieu 16:28, Luc 16:19, Jean 3:1, 5:2, Romains 3:10, al.; with dative (of the possessor; Bl., §37, 3), Matthieu 16:22, Luc 1:7, Jean 18:10, Romains 9:2, al.; ἔστιν ὅς, ὅστις (chiefly in pl), Matthieu 16:28, 19:2, Marc 9:1, al.; 
__(b) with inf., = ἔξεστιν (which see), it is possible: Hébreux 9:5, 1 Corinthiens 11:20, RV (but see ICC, in l.).
__II. As copula uniting subject and predicate. 
__1. Expressing simply identity or equivalence: Matthieu 5:13, 14:15, Luc 1:18, 19, Jean 1:1, 4:19, Apocalypse 3:9, al. mult.
__2. Explicative, as in parable, figure, type, etc.: Matthieu 13:19, 1 Corinthiens 9:2, 10:4, 11:25, Galates 4:24, Apocalypse 17:15, al.; ταῦτ᾽ ἔστιν, Matthieu 27:46, Marc 7:2, Romains 7:18 al.; ὅ ἐστιν, Marc 3:17, Colossiens 1:24, Hébreux 7:2, al.; akin to this is the sacramental usage: Matthieu 26:26-28, Marc 14:22, 24, Luc 22:19, 1 Corinthiens 11:24 (see ICC on Mk, I Co, ll. with; DB, iii, 148 f.). 
__3. C. genitive: qual., etc., Marc 5:42, Luc 3:23, 1 Corinthiens 14:33, Hébreux 12:11, al.; part., 1 Timothée 1:20, 2 Timothée 1:15; poss., Matthieu 5:3, 10, Marc 12:7, Luc 4:7; of service or partisanship, Romains 8:9, 1 Corinthiens 1:12, 2 Corinthiens 10:7, 2 Timothée 2:19. 
__4. C. dative (BL, §37, 3): Actes 1:8, 9:15, Romains 4:12, 1 Corinthiens 1:18, 2:14, Apocalypse 21:7, al. 
__5. C. ptcp., as a periphrasis for the simple verb (Bl., §62, 1, 2; M, Pr., 225 ff.); 
__(a) with ptcp. pf. (cl.): Matthieu 10:30, Luc 9:32, Jean 3:24, Actes 21:35, 1 Corinthiens 15:19, al; 
__(b) with ptcp. pr. (esp. in impf., as in Heb. and Aram.; Dalman, Words, 35 f.), Matthieu 7:29, Marc 1:22, Luc 4:31, 14:1, Actes 1:10, al. mult., id. for imper. (M, Pr., 180f., 182f.), with ellipsis of εἰμί, Romains 12:9, 10, Hébreux 13:5, al.;
__(with) with ptcp. aor. (cl), Luc 23:9.
__6. Seq. εἰς (cf. Heb. הָיָה לְ), a vernac. usage (M, Pr., 71): Matthieu 19:5, Marc 10:8, Hébreux 8:10, al. 
__7. C. adv.: Matthieu 19:20, Marc 4:26, Luc 18:11, al. 
__8. Ellipses; 
__(a) of the copula (Bl., §30, 3): Matthieu 8:29, 24:32, Jean 21:22, 23, Hébreux 6:4, al.;
__(b) of the predicate: ἐγώ εἰμί, Matthieu 14:27, Marc 6:50, al.; absol. (cf. Deutéronome 32:39; אֲנִי הוּא), Marc 13:6, Jean 4:26, al. (cf. ἄπ-, ἔν-, πάρ-, συμ-πάρ-, σύν-ειμι).

G1511.def:
εἰμί, 
