G1519.def:
εἰς, 
prep. with accusative, 
expressing entrance, direction, limit, into, unto, to, upon, towards, for, among (Lat. in, with accusative). 
__I. Of place. 
__1. After verbs of motion; 
__(a) of entrance into: Matthieu 8:23, 9:7, Marc 1:45, Luc 2:15, 8:31, al.; 
__(b) of approach, to or towards: Marc 11:1, Luc 6:8, 19:28, Jean 11:31, 21:6, al.; 
__(with) before pl. and collective nouns, among: Marc 4:7, 8:19, 20, Luc 11:49, Jean 21:23, al.; 
__(d) Of a limit reached, unto, on, upon: Matthieu 8:18, 21:1, Marc 11:1, 13:16, Luc 14:10, Jean 6:3, 11:32, al.; with accusative of person(s) (as in Ep. and Ion.), Actes 23:15, Romains 5:12, 16:19, 2 Corinthiens 10:14; 
__(e) elliptical: ἐπιστολαὶ εἰς Δαμασκόν, Actes 9:2; ἡ διακονία μου ἡ εἰς Ἱ., Romains 15:31; metaphorically, of entrance into a certain state or condition, or of approach or direction towards some end (Thayer, B, i, 1; ii, 1), εἰς τ. ὄνομα, M, Pr., 200. 
__2. Of direction; 
__(a) after verbs of seeing: Matthieu 6:26, Marc 6:41, Luc 9:16, 62, Jean 13:22, al.; metaphorically, of the mind, Hébreux 11:26, 12:2, al.; 
__(b) after verbs of speaking: Matthieu 13:10, 14:9, 1 Thessaloniciens 2:9, al.
__3. After verbs of rest; 
__(a) in "pregnant" construction, implying previous motion (cl.; see WM, 516; Bl., §39, 3; M, Pr., 234f.): Matthieu 2:23, 4:13, 2 Thessaloniciens 2:4, 2 Timothée 1:11, Hébreux 11:9, al.; 
__(b) by an assimilation general in late Gk (see Bl., M, Pr., ll. with) = ἐν: Luc 1:44, 4:23, Actes 20:16, 21:17, Jean 1:18 (but see Westc, in l.), al. 
__II. Of time, for, unto; 
__1. accentuating the duration expressed by the accusative: εἰς τ. αἰῶνα, Matthieu 21:19; εἰς γενεὰς καὶ γ., Luc 1:50; εἰς τ. διηνεκές, Hébreux 7:3, al. 
__2. Of a point or limit of time, unto, up to, until: Matthieu 6:34, Actes 4:3, 25:21, Philippiens 1:10, 2:16, 1 Thessaloniciens 4:15, 2 Timothée 1:12; of entrance into a future period, σεις τὸ μέλλον (see: μέλλω), next (year), Luc 13:9 (but with ICC, in l.); εἰς τ. μεταξὺ σάββατον, on the next Sabbath, Actes 13:42; εἰς τὸ πάλιν (see: πάλιν, 2 Corinthiens 13:2. 
__III. Of result, after verbs of changing, joining, dividing, etc.: στρέφειν εἰς, Apocalypse 11:6; μετας-, Actes 2:20, Jacques 4:9; μεταλλάσσειν, Romains 1:26; σχίζειν εἰς δύο, Matthieu 27:51, al.; predicatively with εἴναι, Actes 8:23. 
__IV. Of relation, to, towards, for, in regard to (so in cl., but more frequently in late Gk., εἰς encroaching on the simple dative, which it has wholly displaced in MGr.; Jannaris, Gr., §1541; Robertson, Gr., 594; Deiss., BS, 117f.): Luc 7:30, Romains 4:20, 15:2, 26, 1 Corinthiens 16:1, Éphésiens 3:16, al.; ἀγάπη εἰς, Romains 5:8, al.; χρηστός, Éphésiens 4:32; φρονεῖν εἰς, Romains 12:16; θαρρεῖν, 2 Corinthiens 10:1. 
__V. Of the end or object: εὔθετος εἰς, Luc 14:34; σόφος, Romains 16:19; ἰσχύειν, Matthieu 5:13; εἰς τοῦτο, Marc 1:38, al.; ἀφορίζειν εἰς, Romains 1:1; indicating purpose, εἰς φόβον, Romains 8:15; εἰς ἔνδειξιν, Romains 3:25; εἰς τό, with inf. (= ἵνα or ὥστε; Bl., §71, 5; M, Pr., 218ff.): Matthieu 20:19, Romains 1:11, 1 Corinthiens 9:18, al. 
__VI. Adverbial phrases: εἰς τέλος, εἰς τὸ πάλιν, etc (see: τέλος, πάλιν, etc.).

G1520.def:
εἷς 
ιά, ἕν, genitive ἑνός, μιᾶς, ἑνός, 
cardinal numeral, one; 
__1. one, as opposite to many: Matthieu 25:15, Romains 5:12, 1 Corinthiens 10:8, al.; as subst., Romains 5:15, Éphésiens 2:14; id. with genitive partit., Matthieu 5:19, al.; before ἐκ (ἐξ), Marc 14:18, Jean 6:8, al.; metaphorically, of union and concord, Jean 10:30 17:11, Romains 12:4-5, Philippiens 1:27; ἀπὸ μιᾶς (B1., § 44, 1), Luc 14:18; with neg., εἷς. . . οὐ (μή), more emphatic than οὐδείς, no one, none (cl.), Matthieu 5:18 10:29, Luc 11:46 12:6. 
__2. Emphatically, to the exclusion of others; 
__(a) a single (one): Matthieu 21:24, Marc 8:14; absol., 1 Corinthiens 9:24, al.; οὐδὲ εἷς, Matthieu 27:14, Jean 1:3, Romains 3:10, al.; 
__(b) one, alone: Marc 2:7 10:18, Luc 18:19; 
__(with) one and the same: Romains 3:30, 1 Corinthiens 3:8 11:5 12:11, 1 Jean 5:8. 
__3. In late Gk., with weakened force, = τις or indef. art. (of. Heb. אֶחָד, Genèse 22:13, al.; see B1., § 45, 2; M, Pr., 96 f.): Matthieu 8:19 19:6, Apocalypse 8:13, al.; εἷς τις (Bl., l.with), Luc 22:50, Jean 11:49 
__4. Distributively: εἷς καστος (cl.), Luc 4:40, Actes 2:6, al.; εἷς . . . καὶ εἷς (cl., εἷς μὲν . . . εἷς δέ), Matthieu 17:4, Marc 9:5, Jean 20:12, al. (cf. LXX and use of Heb. אֶחָד, Exode 17:12, al); ὁ εἷς . . . ὁ ἕτερος (ἄλλος) = cl. ὁ μὲν (ἕτερος) . . . ὁ δέ (ἕτερος), Matthieu 6:24, Luc 7:41, Apocalypse 17:10; καθ᾽ εἷς, εἷς κ. είς (in which καθ᾽ is adverbial, or the expression formed from the analogy of ἕν καθ᾽ ἔν; M, Pr., 105), one by one, severally: Marc 14:19, Romains 12:5, al.; εἷς τὸν ἕνα = ἀλλήλους (B1., 45, 2; M, Pr., 246), 1 Thessaloniciens 5:11. 
__5. As ordinal = πρῶτος (like Heb. אֶחָד; Bl., § 45, 1; M, Pr., 95 f.), first: Matthieu 28:1, Marc 16:2, al

G1553.def:
ἐκ-δημέω, -ῶ
(ἔκδημος, from home; cf. -ία, 3Ma.4:11)*; 
to be from home, absent: 2 Corinthiens 5:6; before ἀπό, 2 Corinthiens 5:8; before ἐκ, 2 Corinthiens 5:9 (cf. ἀπο-, ἐνδημέω).†

G1561.def:
ἐκ-δοχή ῆς, ἡ
(ἐκδέχομαι); 
__1. in cl., 
__(a) a receiving from, succession; 
__(b) an interpretation. 
__2. In NT, = προσδοκία, expectation: Hébreux 10:27 (cf. Field, Notes, 231; Cremer, 688).†

G1577.def:
ἐκκλησία, -ας, ἡ 
(ἐκ-καλέω), [in LXX chiefly for קָהָל, otherwise for one of its cogn. forms ;] 
__1. prop., an assembly of citizens regularly convened (in Thuc., ii, 22, opposite to σύλλογος, a concourse): Actes 19:32, 39 41. 
__2. In LXX of the assembly, congregation, community of Israel (Deutéronome 4:10 23:2, al.): Actes 7:38, Hébreux 2:12" (LXX) . 
__3. NT, esp. of an assembly or company of Christians, a (the) church; 
__(a) of gatherings for worship: 1 Corinthiens 11:18 14:19, 34 35; 
__(b) of local communities: Actes 8:3, 1 Corinthiens 4:17; with name added, Actes 8:1, Romains 16:1, 1 Thessaloniciens 1:1, al.; pl., Actes 15:41, 1 Corinthiens 7:17; τ. Χριστοῦ, Romains 16:16; τ. Ἀσίας, 1 Corinthiens 16:19; τ. ἁγίων, 1 Corinthiens 14:33; εἰπο]ν τ. ἐκκλησίᾳ, Matthieu 18:17 (but see Hort, Ecclesia, 10); of a house-congregation (DB, i, 431a), Romains 16:5, 1 Corinthiens 16:19, Colossiens 4:15, Phm 2; 
__(with) of the whole body of Christians: Matthieu 16:18, 1 Corinthiens 12:28, Éphésiens 1:22, Philippiens 3:6, al.; τ. θεοῦ, Actes 20:28 (Κυρίου, T, R, mg.), 1 Corinthiens 15:9, Galates 1:13, 1 Timothée 3:15; ἐ. προτοτόκων ἀπογεγραμμένων ἐν οὐρανοῖς, Hébreux 12:23. 
SYN.: συναγωγή, which see (see Tr., Syn., §i; DB, i, 426; Hort, Ecclesia, esp. 4ff., 107ff.; Hamilton, People of God, ii, 37ff.; reff. s.vv. "Church," "Congregation," in DB and DCG; Cremer, 332).

G1588.def:
ἐκ-λεκτός, -ή, -όν 
(ἐκλέγω), [in LXX for בָּחַר (so prob. in Ésaïe 28:16, Proverbes 17:3, for MT בָּחַן), בָּרִיא, etc. ;] 
__1. choice, select (cl., rarely; Thuc., Plat., al.), hence, eminent: Romains 16:13 (cf. Eze.27:24). 
__2. As in Inscr. (MM, Exp., xii), chosen; esp. as in LXX, of Israel, elect, chosen of God (Ésaïe 65:9, Psaumes 105:43, al.); so in NT; 
__(a) of Christ: Luc 23:35 (cf. Ésaïe 42:1); figuratively, λίθος, 1 Pierre 2:4-6 (LXX); 
__(b) of holy angels: 1 Timothée 5:21; 
__(with) of Christians: Matthieu 24:22, 24, Marc 13:20, 22 13:27, 2 Timothée 2:10, 1 Pierre 1:1; τ. θεοῦ, Luc 18:7, Romains 8:33, Colossiens 3:12, Tite 1:1; τ. Χριστοῦ, Matthieu 24:31; ἐ. κυρία, II Jn 1; ἀδελφή, II Jn 13; γένος, 1 Pierre 2:9 (LXX); κλητοὶ καὶ ἐ. κ. πιστοί, Apocalypse 17:14; opposite to κλητός (not so in Epp.; see Lft. on Colossiens 3:12), Matthieu 20:16 (T, WH, txt., R, omit) Matthieu 22:14 (Cremer, 405, 775).†
